#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0168 expect=noViolation domain=ADLB
#note "Non-firing counterpart: 201/GLUC keeps the filter-discriminating pair (post-baseline ANRIND 'NORMAL' sorts above baseline 'HIGH', BNRIND='HIGH' everywhere - a filter-ignoring max() would false-fire and red this scenario) and 203/GLUC keeps only the empty-BNRIND no-baseline row, held quiet by the non_empty guard."
#library standard=adamig version=1-2
dataset ADLB label="Analysis Dataset Lab"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PARAMCD  type=Char label="Parameter Code"
col AVISITN  type=Num  label="Analysis Visit (N)"
col BASETYPE type=Char label="Baseline Type"
col ABLFL    type=Char label="Baseline Record Flag"
col ANRIND   type=Char label="Analysis Reference Range Indicator"
col BNRIND   type=Char label="Baseline Reference Range Indicator"
---
S1 | 201 | GLUC | 0 | LAST | Y | HIGH   | HIGH
S1 | 201 | GLUC | 1 | LAST |   | NORMAL | HIGH
S1 | 203 | GLUC | 2 | LAST |   | LOW    |
